From: pocket-debs <masterxq@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 19:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] plugins: sliding effects: do not keep closed windows that are not painted
Description:
 The slidingnotifications and slidingpopups effects advance their
 animations in prePaintWindow(), which is only called for windows that
 are painted. A window that is not visible, e.g. any window other than
 the lock screen while the session is locked, is never painted, so an
 animation started for it never finishes. For a closed window the effect
 holds an EffectWindowDeletedRef until the animation ends: the closed
 window stays alive and its surface item keeps a reference to the last
 buffer the client attached.
 .
 A client that hides and shows the same wl_surface (Qt keeps the surface
 and its EGL swapchain across hide/show) commits a new buffer on every
 show. Notification popups that come and go while the screen is locked
 thus pile up closed windows, each holding one buffer of the swapchain.
 Once all of them are held, Mesa's EGL waits for a buffer release that
 never comes and the client hangs in eglMakeCurrent()/eglSwapBuffers().
 plasmashell on Plasma Mobile hung this way after four notifications on
 the lock screen.
 .
 Do not start a close animation for a window that is not visible and
 drop the animation it may still have. slidingnotifications also stops
 its animations when the screen locking state changes, as slidingpopups
 already does.
Author: masterxq <masterxq@users.noreply.github.com>
Forwarded: no
License: GPL-2.0-or-later (as the patched files)
Last-Update: 2026-11-28
---
diff --git a/src/plugins/slidingnotifications/slidingnotifications.cpp b/src/plugins/slidingnotifications/slidingnotifications.cpp
index fc5cfdca..2e948889 100644
--- a/src/plugins/slidingnotifications/slidingnotifications.cpp
+++ b/src/plugins/slidingnotifications/slidingnotifications.cpp
@@ -381,6 +381,9 @@ SlidingNotificationsEffect::SlidingNotificationsEffect()
 {
     connect(effects, &EffectsHandler::windowAdded, this, &SlidingNotificationsEffect::onWindowAdded);
     connect(effects, &EffectsHandler::windowClosed, this, &SlidingNotificationsEffect::onWindowClosed);
+    connect(effects, &EffectsHandler::screenLockingChanged, this, [this]() {
+        m_animations.clear();
+    });
 }
 
 bool SlidingNotificationsEffect::isActive() const
@@ -484,6 +487,13 @@ void SlidingNotificationsEffect::onWindowClosed(EffectWindow *window)
         return;
     }
 
+    // Animations advance only while the window is painted, which a window that is not visible (e.g. on
+    // a locked screen) is not. The animation would keep the closed window and its last buffer forever.
+    if (!window->windowItem()->isVisible()) {
+        m_animations.erase(window);
+        return;
+    }
+
     window->setData(WindowClosedGrabRole, QVariant::fromValue(static_cast<void *>(this)));
 
     auto &animation = m_animations[window];
diff --git a/src/plugins/slidingpopups/slidingpopups.cpp b/src/plugins/slidingpopups/slidingpopups.cpp
index fc931f24..e8e36d2a 100644
--- a/src/plugins/slidingpopups/slidingpopups.cpp
+++ b/src/plugins/slidingpopups/slidingpopups.cpp
@@ -474,6 +474,13 @@ void SlidingPopupsEffect::slideOut(EffectWindow *w)
         return;
     }
 
+    // The animation advances only while the window is painted, which a window that is not visible
+    // (e.g. on a locked screen) is not. It would keep the closed window and its last buffer forever.
+    if (!w->windowItem()->isVisible()) {
+        m_animations.erase(w);
+        return;
+    }
+
     auto dataIt = m_animationsData.constFind(w);
     if (dataIt == m_animationsData.constEnd()) {
         return;
